ARTICLE I — ON OWNERSHIP
  This software is mine. I made it, largely by telling a computer it was
  wrong until it stopped being wrong.

ARTICLE II — ON LOOKING
  You may not look at it. Not the source, not the comments, not this
  sentence. If you have read this far you are already in breach.

ARTICLE III — ON EVERYTHING ELSE
  Well. *Officially...*

  You may not use it, copy it, modify it, ship it, sell it, fold it into
  a product, or otherwise treat it as yours. No touching it. No licking
  it. No tickling it. No permission is granted for any of that. None. Not
  a little. Not for a good cause.

ARTICLE IV — ON ENFORCEMENT
  If you do it anyway you are a space pirate, and we both know there is no
  space police. You go on the list. It is a long list, it is kept badly,
  and nobody has ever read it.

ARTICLE V — ON WARRANTY
  There isn't one. THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF
  ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED. If it eats your patches, bricks your
  synth, or produces a sound that cannot afterwards be unheard, that is
  between you and the sound.


- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

  and here comes the legal slop, because not even I am a true space pirate

Articles I to V cover only the parts of this repository that I wrote. They
do not reach the work it is built on, and they could not even if I wanted
them to: those authors granted rights that are not mine to take back.

In particular, the DX7 synthesis engine under src/engine/ is a port of
msfa and is licensed under Apache License 2.0 by Google Inc. and Pascal
Gauthier. You may use, copy, modify and redistribute that code under those
terms regardless of anything written above. The patch data shipped in
public/bundles/ is released into the public domain under CC0 1.0 and is
likewise free for anyone to take.

The full list, with the notices those licences require, is in
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md, and a copy of the Apache licence is in licenses/.

So: plunder my half if you must. The engine was never mine to guard.
